{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:d5d2c600dee47212","name":"Ship Gunner","source":{"id":"source:reference-d5d2c600dee47212","title":"Ship Gunner","revision":19024,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:09:37Z","sha256":"e6c754f6d0ce32b5289d18241524910d5781e2be2e24ec9a4808623545e206f3","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19024","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Ship%20Gunner&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-d5d2c600dee47212","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Ship Gunner controls one or more ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"}," not directly under the control of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"},". Typical sorts of weapons a Ship Gunner might employ include the composite-beam laser on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["LAAT/i Gunship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/LAAT/i_Gunship","referenceId":"reference:4ec307279de7b7a7"}," or the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Cannon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Cannon","referenceId":"reference:ae1584087cb7657b"}," on the ",{"tag":"a","children":["T-47 Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/T-47_Airspeeder"},". In most cases, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," retains control over some of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"},", but the Gunner's role is largely to free up the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," to maneuver the ship, while the Ship Gunner unleashes a torrent of fire against enemy ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Ship Gunners are prevalent in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," of just about any size and can also be found operating the batteries on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ground Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ground_Vehicles"}," and other atmospheric craft. Most armored assault ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Walkers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Walkers","referenceId":"reference:552672704065a9f2"}," include a broad spectrum of weapons and might employ multiple Ship Gunners.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Ship Gunner Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Ship Gunners appear in skirmishes involving armored ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," or large-scale space battles. Gunners function as part of a ship's crew, and a ship with a full crew complement will have at least one Ship Gunner for each ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," position on the vessel. In these cases, the Gunner's most vital attribute is their attack bonus, with their other statistics rarely coming into play. This said, most Ship Gunners are pilots as well, and they can fill in for a wounded or dead ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Copilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Copilot","referenceId":"reference:49f5b0e488cfa66c"}," as needed.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In atmospheric encounters, Ship Gunners function in much the same way, usually as part of a Walker's or armored assault Vehicle's crew. Again, a Ship Gunner can also serve as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," and might be called upon to fill in for an injured comrade. Should the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," be disabled, a Ship Gunner is an effective combatant and fights along with the rest of the surviving crew. A Ship Gunner's training with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heavy Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heavy_Weapons","referenceId":"reference:a2b1d4c4bac82300"}," allows such a character to perform double duty and function as heavy infantry when needed, laying down suppressive fire with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Cannon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Cannon","referenceId":"reference:ae1584087cb7657b"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Missile Launcher"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Missile_Launcher","referenceId":"reference:f5c813188b5889e5"}," as the situation demands.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Ship Gunner Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 4/",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"}," 3/",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +7; ",{"tag":"b","ch